ServiceNow CAD
300-Question Mock Exam
Six practice tests, 50 questions each, with answer keys and concise explanations
Blueprint distributionQuestions
Designing and Creating an Application60
Application User Interface60
Security and Restricting Access60
Application Automation60
Working with External Data30
Managing Applications30
How to use this book
Take one 50-question test at a time. Select one best answer for each item, then score yourself with the answer key. These are original,
unofficial practice questions and are not copied from the live certification exam.
The question mix follows the January 2026 blueprint: Designing and Creating an Application 20%; Application User Interface 20%; Security and
Restricting Access 20%; Application Automation 20%; Working with External Data 10%; Managing Applications 10%.

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 2
Practice Test 1
50 questions | Suggested time: 70 minutes | Choose one best answer.
1. Which option is the BEST practice for reference field?
A. Use a Reference field to relate a record to one record on another table
B. Use a Choice field to store a sys_id manually
C. Use an HTML field to enforce referential integrity
D. Use a Journal field for relational joins
2. Which option is the BEST practice for client-callable include?
A. Mark and design a Script Include appropriately for controlled GlideAjax use
B. Put server secrets into the client script
C. Return unrestricted records to any caller
D. Make every Script Include public without validation
3. Which option is the BEST practice for field type?
A. Choose field types based on the data and required behavior, such as Date/Time, Reference, or Choice
B. Use String for every field regardless of purpose
C. Use Journal for numeric calculations
D. Use HTML for all relationships
4. Which option is the BEST practice for Debug Security Rules?
A. Use an import set log for client ACLs
B. Use Debug Security Rules to see which ACLs pass or fail for an access attempt
C. Use Schema Map to trace ACL execution
D. Use Form Designer to grant roles
5. Which option is the BEST practice for business rule?
A. Use a Client Script for background imports with no browser
B. Use a Business Rule for server-side logic triggered by database operations
C. Use a module as a database trigger
D. Use CSS for data validation on insert
6. Which option is the BEST practice for dictionary attributes?
A. Put all field behavior in a module title
B. Edit the database directly outside ServiceNow
C. Configure field behavior through the dictionary entry and appropriate attributes
D. Use only browser CSS to define the data type
7. Which option is the BEST practice for async rule?
A. Use an async Business Rule for non-immediate server work that should not delay the user transaction
B. Use it when the user must see an immediate blocking error
C. Use it to set mandatory fields in the browser
D. Use it to control module visibility
8. Which option is the BEST practice for application property?
A. Use table labels as passwords
B. Store configurable application behavior in an application property and retrieve it with the appropriate API
C. Hard-code environment-specific values throughout scripts
D. Create a new field for every configuration flag

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 3
9. Which option is the BEST practice for transform map?
A. Use a Transform Map to define how source fields populate target fields
B. Use a form section as a field map
C. Use an ACL to rename CSV headers
D. Use a Client Script to map spreadsheet columns during a background import
10. Which option is the BEST practice for table extension?
A. Duplicate every field into an unrelated table
B. Use extension only to change a form label
C. Extend an existing table when the new records need its inherited fields and behavior
D. Extend a table to bypass all ACL evaluation
11. Which option is the BEST practice for Flow Designer?
A. Use Flow Designer for maintainable trigger-and-action automation where supported
B. Use a schema map to schedule tasks
C. Use a form layout as a process engine
D. Use an ACL to send all notifications
12. Which option is the BEST practice for inbound email action?
A. Use an ACL to create email records
B. Use a form layout to receive SMTP
C. Use an outbound notification to parse incoming mail
D. Use an Inbound Email Action or email flow to process qualifying incoming messages
13. Which option is the BEST practice for module visibility?
A. Use a form section to grant access
B. Rely on module roles as the only protection for table records
C. Use list sorting to hide unauthorized data
D. Assign roles to application menus or modules to limit navigation visibility
14. Which option is the BEST practice for onChange?
A. Use an onChange Client Script when logic should run after a field value changes
B. Use onLoad only after every field change
C. Use a Business Rule that requires form reload for all UI feedback
D. Use an inbound email action
15. Which option is the BEST practice for after rule?
A. Use a dictionary label to trigger integrations
B. Use a module to create audit entries
C. Use an onLoad Client Script for server-side related updates
D. Use an after Business Rule when related records should be updated after the current record is committed
16. Which option is the BEST practice for application access?
A. Configure table Application Access settings to control cross-scope operations
B. Use auto-numbering to block other scopes
C. Use a report filter as the security boundary
D. Use a UI Action label to control cross-scope calls

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 4
17. Which option is the BEST practice for ACL purpose?
A. Use module order to prevent API access
B. Use Access Control rules to authorize operations on tables, records, and fields
C. Use UI Policies as the primary data security layer
D. Hide a field on one form and assume the data is secure
18. Which option is the BEST practice for REST Message?
A. Use a UI Policy to call every external API
B. Use a schema map as the HTTP client
C. Create a REST Message with methods, endpoint, authentication, headers, and parameters for outbound REST
D. Store the endpoint in a form label only
19. Which option is the BEST practice for before rule?
A. Use an async rule to block the user immediately
B. Use a display rule to import CSV data
C. Use a before Business Rule to change the current record before it is saved
D. Use an after rule when the value must be written without another update
20. Which option is the BEST practice for application fit?
A. A static public brochure with no platform data
B. A one-time calculation best handled in a spreadsheet
C. A repeatable business process needing structured records, workflow, security, and reporting
D. A hardware driver that must run in the operating system
21. Which option is the BEST practice for branching?
A. Have every developer overwrite the same branch without coordination
B. Use branching to bypass code review
C. Create a branch for each record update automatically
D. Use branches deliberately and avoid conflicting instance work when collaborating
22. Which option is the BEST practice for UI policy?
A. Use an ACL only to change field color
B. Use a Transform Map for form visibility
C. Use a REST Message for mandatory fields
D. Use a UI Policy for condition-based mandatory, visible, or read-only behavior without scripting when possible
23. Which option is the BEST practice for commit?
A. Commit coherent application changes with a meaningful message
B. Commit random partial changes with no context
C. Include passwords to simplify deployment
D. Use commits to delete audit history
24. Which option is the BEST practice for transform scripts?
A. Put credentials in the source file
B. Use transform scripts for controlled import logic that cannot be handled by direct field maps
C. Use client-only g_form methods during a background transform
D. Disable target validation permanently

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 5
25. Which option is the BEST practice for scheduled execution?
A. Use a form section as a timer
B. Use an onChange Client Script when no user is online
C. Use a UI Policy as a nightly batch
D. Use Scheduled Script Execution for server-side work that must run at a defined time or interval
26. Which option is the BEST practice for flow action?
A. Use reusable actions or subflows for logic shared across automations
B. Put credentials directly into action labels
C. Use module titles as reusable code
D. Copy long logic into every flow
27. Which option is the BEST practice for ACL evaluation?
A. ACLs run only for administrators
B. Form visibility overrides ACLs
C. A user must satisfy the applicable ACL requirements for the requested operation
D. Passing one unrelated ACL grants all access
28. Which option is the BEST practice for table creation?
A. Use a system property as the primary record store
B. Create a custom table and define fields that model the business records
C. Create only a module and avoid a table
D. Store every value in one long string field
29. Which option is the BEST practice for application scope?
A. Scope automatically grants every role access
B. Scope changes the instance time zone
C. Use a scoped application to namespace artifacts and control cross-scope access
D. Use global scope so no protections apply
30. Which option is the BEST practice for import set?
A. Use a module as a staging table
B. Use a UI Policy to parse CSV rows
C. Import every file directly into arbitrary production columns with no mapping
D. Load external file data into an import set table before transforming it to a target table
31. Which option is the BEST practice for source control?
A. Link a scoped application to a supported Git repository to manage application versions
B. Commit production credentials with the application
C. Use Git to store arbitrary instance records automatically
D. Use source control as a replacement for ACLs
32. Which option is the BEST practice for Script Include?
A. Store executable code in a choice label
B. Use a module as a function library
C. Put reusable server-side functions in a Script Include
D. Duplicate the same function in every Business Rule

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 6
33. Which option is the BEST practice for notification event?
A. Use an ACL to format email
B. Use a dictionary override to create recipients
C. Configure a notification to respond to an event when decoupling notification logic is useful
D. Send mail directly from every client script
34. Which option is the BEST practice for onSubmit?
A. Use an onLoad script to cancel every save
B. Use a module visibility rule
C. Use an onSubmit Client Script to prevent submission when client-side conditions fail
D. Use a Scheduled Job to validate before submit
35. Which option is the BEST practice for flow trigger?
A. Use an index as an email trigger
B. Use a field label as the only trigger
C. Define a trigger that clearly identifies when the flow should start
D. Start every flow manually from a browser console
36. Which option is the BEST practice for impersonation testing?
A. Assume module visibility proves record access
B. Disable security before each test
C. Test only while logged in as admin
D. Impersonate a representative non-admin user to test actual access behavior
37. Which option is the BEST practice for GlideAjax?
A. Use GlideAjax to call a client-callable Script Include for server data without reloading the form
B. Use a UI Policy to query remote tables
C. Expose administrator credentials in JavaScript
D. Use synchronous GlideRecord in the browser
38. Which option is the BEST practice for g_form?
A. Use GlideRecord directly from ordinary client code
B. Use g_form in client-side scripts to get or set form values and properties
C. Use current in a browser Client Script
D. Use gs in client-only code
39. Which option is the BEST practice for choice field?
A. Use an Attachment field for option values
B. Use a Choice field for a controlled set of stable values
C. Use free text when consistent reporting is required
D. Use a Reference field without a related table
40. Which option is the BEST practice for pull/conflict?
A. Pull remote changes and resolve source control conflicts carefully before continuing
B. Ignore conflicts and force overwrite every time
C. Use a UI Policy to merge Git branches
D. Resolve conflict by disabling the application

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 7
41. Which option is the BEST practice for event queue?
A. Use gs.eventQueue() to place an event on the event queue for downstream processing
B. Use g_form.addInfoMessage() to create a server event
C. Use the schema map to queue jobs
D. Use a module to fire notifications
42. Which option is the BEST practice for client script?
A. Use a Scheduled Script Execution for immediate form interaction
B. Use a module to validate typed characters
C. Use a Client Script for browser-side form behavior such as reacting to field changes
D. Use an ACL to set a field value onChange
43. Which option is the BEST practice for least privilege?
A. Grant only the roles and privileges required for the user or application task
B. Give admin to avoid troubleshooting authorization
C. Expose records publicly and filter them in the UI
D. Put all users in the same elevated group
44. Which option is the BEST practice for many-to-many?
A. Create a system property for each relationship
B. Add hundreds of true/false fields
C. Use a many-to-many table when records on both sides can relate to multiple records
D. Put comma-separated sys_ids in a string field
45. Which option is the BEST practice for role check?
A. Use g_form.hasRole() in a Business Rule
B. Compare the user name to a hard-coded password
C. Use gs.hasRole() in appropriate server-side security logic to test roles
D. Store roles in a client-visible variable and trust it
46. Which option is the BEST practice for field ACL?
A. Use a client script to erase the field visually
B. Create only a module title condition
C. Create a field ACL when access to a specific field must be more restrictive than table access
D. Use a UI Policy as confidential-data protection
47. Which option is the BEST practice for module purpose?
A. Use a module instead of an ACL
B. Create a module to store table data
C. Use a module as a server-side API
D. Create an application module to give users navigation to a list, record, or page
48. Which option is the BEST practice for coalesce?
A. Mark suitable transform map fields as coalesce to identify matching target records
B. Coalesce every field so no record can transform
C. Use coalesce only to change form labels
D. Use a journal field as a universal key

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 8
49. Which option is the BEST practice for cross-scope privilege?
A. Move all artifacts to global scope
B. Allow every application unrestricted access by default
C. Review and grant only required cross-scope application access privileges
D. Disable application scope security
50. Which option is the BEST practice for delegated development?
A. Use module visibility as developer authorization
B. Use delegated development permissions to let approved developers work on an application without full admin
C. Grant admin to every contributor
D. Use delegated development to expose all global applications

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 9
Practice Test 1 - Answer Key
1. A - A Reference field stores a link to a record on another table. [Designing and Creating an Application]
2. A - Client-callable Script Includes should expose only validated, necessary data. [Application Automation]
3. A - Correct field types improve validation, querying, and user experience. [Designing and Creating an Application]
4. B - Debug Security Rules shows ACL evaluation details. [Security and Restricting Access]
5. B - Business Rules run server-side around record operations. [Application User Interface]
6. C - Dictionary entries define field metadata and platform behavior. [Designing and Creating an Application]
7. A - Async rules run later and reduce transaction response time. [Application User Interface]
8. B - Application properties centralize configuration outside code. [Application Automation]
9. A - Transform Maps control source-to-target field mapping. [Working with External Data]
10. C - Table extension supports reuse of fields and behavior through inheritance. [Designing and Creating an Application]
11. A - Flow Designer provides low-code process automation. [Application Automation]
12. D - Inbound email processing can create or update application records. [Application Automation]
13. D - Module roles control navigation, while ACLs must still protect the data. [Security and Restricting Access]
14. A - onChange is designed for field-change behavior on forms. [Application User Interface]
15. D - After rules are suitable for actions that depend on a completed save. [Application User Interface]
16. A - Application Access settings define permitted operations from other scopes. [Security and Restricting Access]
17. B - ACLs enforce server-side access to data and operations. [Security and Restricting Access]
18. C - REST Messages organize outbound REST integration configuration. [Working with External Data]
19. C - Before rules efficiently modify the record being saved. [Application User Interface]
20. C - ServiceNow applications are strongest for structured, repeatable workflows that benefit from platform services. [Designing and
Creating an Application]
21. D - A clear branching strategy helps control parallel development. [Managing Applications]
22. D - UI Policies provide declarative form behavior. [Application User Interface]
23. A - Focused commits improve traceability and review. [Managing Applications]
24. B - Transform scripts support server-side import customization. [Working with External Data]
25. D - Scheduled Script Executions run server code on a schedule. [Application Automation]
26. A - Reusable actions and subflows improve consistency and maintenance. [Application Automation]
27. C - ACL evaluation protects access across interfaces, not just forms. [Security and Restricting Access]
28. B - A table with appropriately typed fields provides a maintainable data model. [Designing and Creating an Application]
29. C - Application scope isolates and protects application artifacts. [Designing and Creating an Application]
30. D - Import sets provide a staging area for external data. [Working with External Data]
31. A - ServiceNow source control integration manages scoped application files and versions. [Managing Applications]
32. C - Script Includes promote reusable server-side logic. [Application Automation]
33. C - Event-driven notifications separate business logic from communication. [Application Automation]
34. C - onSubmit can return false to stop form submission. [Application User Interface]
35. C - A flow requires a valid trigger such as record creation, update, schedule, or application event. [Application Automation]
36. D - Impersonation helps validate the effective user experience and permissions. [Security and Restricting Access]
37. A - GlideAjax provides controlled asynchronous client-to-server calls. [Application User Interface]
38. B - g_form is the standard client-side form API. [Application User Interface]
39. B - Choice fields standardize allowed values and improve reporting. [Designing and Creating an Application]
40. A - Conflict resolution protects the intended application state. [Managing Applications]
41. A - gs.eventQueue() is used server-side to generate events. [Application Automation]

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 10
42. C - Client Scripts run in the browser and can respond to form events. [Application User Interface]
43. A - Least privilege reduces unnecessary access and risk. [Security and Restricting Access]
44. C - A junction table is the normalized design for many-to-many relationships. [Designing and Creating an Application]
45. C - gs.hasRole() is a server-side role check, though ACL roles should be used directly when possible. [Security and Restricting
Access]
46. C - Field ACLs enforce server-side field access. [Security and Restricting Access]
47. D - Modules are navigation entries within an application menu. [Designing and Creating an Application]
48. A - Coalesce fields determine whether a transform updates an existing record or inserts a new one. [Working with External Data]
49. C - Cross-scope privileges control access between scoped applications. [Security and Restricting Access]
50. B - Delegated development provides controlled development access. [Managing Applications]

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 11
Practice Test 2
50 questions | Suggested time: 70 minutes | Choose one best answer.
1. A developer is working on transform map. What should the developer do?
A. Use an ACL to rename CSV headers
B. Use a Client Script to map spreadsheet columns during a background import
C. Use a form section as a field map
D. Use a Transform Map to define how source fields populate target fields
2. Which option is the BEST practice for HTTP status?
A. Ignore 400 and 500 responses
B. Assume only 200 can ever be successful
C. Handle expected success and error HTTP status codes explicitly
D. Parse the response before checking whether the request failed
3. Which option is the BEST practice for record producer?
A. Use it only to delete tables
B. Use it as a database index
C. Use it to replace all ACLs
D. Use a Record Producer to let users create records through a catalog-style interface
4. Which option is the BEST practice for flow testing?
A. Test a flow with representative input, inspect each step, and confirm resulting records
B. Publish directly to production without a test
C. Disable error handling during validation
D. Judge success only by the flow name
5. Which option is the BEST practice for client diagnostics?
A. Use browser developer tools and ServiceNow client-side debugging tools to inspect client errors
B. Use an email notification to display stack traces
C. Use an update set preview as the only client debugger
D. Use database indexes to read JavaScript console errors
6. A developer is working on table extension. What should the developer do?
A. Duplicate every field into an unrelated table
B. Use extension only to change a form label
C. Extend an existing table when the new records need its inherited fields and behavior
D. Extend a table to bypass all ACL evaluation
7. A developer is working on import set. What should the developer do?
A. Use a module as a staging table
B. Use a UI Policy to parse CSV rows
C. Import every file directly into arbitrary production columns with no mapping
D. Load external file data into an import set table before transforming it to a target table
8. Which option is the BEST practice for admin override?
A. Understand the ACL admin override setting and test behavior intentionally
B. Assume admin override can never be changed
C. Use admin override to grant anonymous access
D. The setting controls only form color

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 12
9. Which option is the BEST practice for code review?
A. Use code review to inspect changes for quality, security, scope, and maintainability
B. Skip review for server-side security scripts
C. Review only labels and ignore logic
D. Approve changes based only on file count
10. A developer is working on onChange. What should the developer do?
A. Use an inbound email action
B. Use an onChange Client Script when logic should run after a field value changes
C. Use a Business Rule that requires form reload for all UI feedback
D. Use onLoad only after every field change
11. Which option is the BEST practice for workflow context?
A. Disable logging and retry blindly
B. Use only the browser color theme to debug
C. Inspect flow execution details or workflow context when diagnosing automation
D. Delete all execution records before review
12. A developer is working on table creation. What should the developer do?
A. Create only a module and avoid a table
B. Use a system property as the primary record store
C. Store every value in one long string field
D. Create a custom table and define fields that model the business records
13. A developer is working on client script. What should the developer do?
A. Use a Scheduled Script Execution for immediate form interaction
B. Use a Client Script for browser-side form behavior such as reacting to field changes
C. Use a module to validate typed characters
D. Use an ACL to set a field value onChange
14. Which option is the BEST practice for application install?
A. Copy random XML files from unknown sources
B. Install directly without checking target release
C. Install applications from the appropriate ServiceNow source and review dependencies and compatibility
D. Use a client script to install plugins
15. Which option is the BEST practice for credentials?
A. Email credentials to every developer
B. Use ServiceNow credential and connection mechanisms instead of hard-coding secrets in scripts
C. Put usernames and passwords in client scripts
D. Store tokens in module names
16. A developer is working on g_form. What should the developer do?
A. Use g_form in client-side scripts to get or set form values and properties
B. Use current in a browser Client Script
C. Use gs in client-only code
D. Use GlideRecord directly from ordinary client code

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 13
17. Which option is the BEST practice for email recipients?
A. Use a table index as an email address
B. Send all application mail to every user
C. Hard-code a personal email in every script
D. Use data-driven recipient fields, groups, or event parameters and validate who should receive the message
18. A developer is working on onSubmit. What should the developer do?
A. Use a Scheduled Job to validate before submit
B. Use an onSubmit Client Script to prevent submission when client-side conditions fail
C. Use a module visibility rule
D. Use an onLoad script to cancel every save
19. Which option is the BEST practice for auto-number?
A. Use the sys_updated_on value as the display number
B. Configure an auto-number when each record needs a readable unique identifier
C. Use the record short description as the guaranteed unique key
D. Ask users to invent identifiers with no validation
20. A developer is working on Debug Security Rules. What should the developer do?
A. Use Schema Map to trace ACL execution
B. Use Form Designer to grant roles
C. Use Debug Security Rules to see which ACLs pass or fail for an access attempt
D. Use an import set log for client ACLs
21. A developer is working on event queue. What should the developer do?
A. Use a module to fire notifications
B. Use gs.eventQueue() to place an event on the event queue for downstream processing
C. Use the schema map to queue jobs
D. Use g_form.addInfoMessage() to create a server event
22. A developer is working on reference field. What should the developer do?
A. Use an HTML field to enforce referential integrity
B. Use a Journal field for relational joins
C. Use a Reference field to relate a record to one record on another table
D. Use a Choice field to store a sys_id manually
23. A developer is working on role check. What should the developer do?
A. Compare the user name to a hard-coded password
B. Use g_form.hasRole() in a Business Rule
C. Use gs.hasRole() in appropriate server-side security logic to test roles
D. Store roles in a client-visible variable and trust it
24. Which option is the BEST practice for schema map?
A. Use it to encrypt attachments
B. Use Schema Map to visualize table relationships and extensions
C. Use it to impersonate users
D. Use it to execute production scripts

