25. Which option is the BEST practice for record ownership?
A. Hide the Assigned to field and allow all reads
B. Use a choice value as a password
C. Use an ACL condition or script to compare the record with the current user when ownership matters
D. Use form color to indicate privacy
26. Which option is the BEST practice for server script debugging?
A. Use Script Debugger, logs, and appropriate test records to inspect server-side behavior
B. Disable all ACLs permanently
C. Use browser CSS to trace Business Rules
D. Change production data randomly until it works
27. Which option is the BEST practice for script ACL?
A. Use an ACL script when authorization depends on logic not covered by roles or conditions alone
B. Use a transform map for interactive reads
C. Use an email template to check access
D. Use a Client Script because it cannot be bypassed
28. A developer is working on application property. What should the developer do?
A. Hard-code environment-specific values throughout scripts
B. Store configurable application behavior in an application property and retrieve it with the appropriate API
C. Use table labels as passwords
D. Create a new field for every configuration flag
29. A developer is working on impersonation testing. What should the developer do?
A. Assume module visibility proves record access
B. Disable security before each test
C. Impersonate a representative non-admin user to test actual access behavior
D. Test only while logged in as admin
30. A developer is working on UI policy. What should the developer do?
A. Use a Transform Map for form visibility
B. Use a UI Policy for condition-based mandatory, visible, or read-only behavior without scripting when possible
C. Use an ACL only to change field color
D. Use a REST Message for mandatory fields
31. Which option is the BEST practice for number field?
A. Use a String field and rely on users to type numbers correctly
B. Use a Journal field for arithmetic
C. Use an Integer, Decimal, or Currency field when numeric operations and validation are needed
D. Use a Reference field with no target table
32. A developer is working on many-to-many. What should the developer do?
A. Use a many-to-many table when records on both sides can relate to multiple records
B. Create a system property for each relationship
C. Put comma-separated sys_ids in a string field
D. Add hundreds of true/false fields

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 15
33. Which option is the BEST practice for recursion avoidance?
A. Convert every rule into a client script
B. Avoid unnecessary current.update() calls inside Business Rules on the same record
C. Disable all Business Rules globally
D. Use repeated updates to guarantee correctness
34. A developer is working on flow action. What should the developer do?
A. Put credentials directly into action labels
B. Use reusable actions or subflows for logic shared across automations
C. Copy long logic into every flow
D. Use module titles as reusable code
35. Which option is the BEST practice for order of operations?
A. Call current.update() in every Business Rule
B. Ignore whether logic runs before or after persistence
C. Consider Business Rule timing and automation interactions to avoid recursion and unintended updates
D. Place identical logic in multiple engines
36. Which option is the BEST practice for data model normalization?
A. Create duplicate tables for each user
B. Copy the same customer details into every transaction record
C. Store all records in one unstructured text field
D. Separate reusable entities into related tables instead of repeating the same attributes
37. A developer is working on branching. What should the developer do?
A. Have every developer overwrite the same branch without coordination
B. Use branching to bypass code review
C. Create a branch for each record update automatically
D. Use branches deliberately and avoid conflicting instance work when collaborating
38. Which option is the BEST practice for deployment validation?
A. Validate only that the application menu exists
B. After deployment, run smoke tests for key roles, data access, automations, and integrations
C. Assume a successful install means all functions work
D. Test only as admin
39. Which option is the BEST practice for REST testing?
A. Test a REST method with safe sample data and inspect status, headers, and response body
B. Treat any HTTP response as success
C. Ignore authentication errors and retry endlessly
D. Test destructive calls first in production
40. A developer is working on ACL purpose. What should the developer do?
A. Use module order to prevent API access
B. Use UI Policies as the primary data security layer
C. Hide a field on one form and assume the data is secure
D. Use Access Control rules to authorize operations on tables, records, and fields

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 16
41. A developer is working on flow trigger. What should the developer do?
A. Use an index as an email trigger
B. Start every flow manually from a browser console
C. Use a field label as the only trigger
D. Define a trigger that clearly identifies when the flow should start
42. Which option is the BEST practice for secure server API?
A. Perform sensitive validation and authorization on the server even when client checks exist
B. Send privileged decisions entirely to the client
C. Trust hidden client variables for authorization
