1. A - Transform Maps control source-to-target field mapping. [Working with External Data]
2. C - onSubmit can return false to stop form submission. [Application User Interface]
3. A - Client-callable Script Includes should expose only validated, necessary data. [Application Automation]
4. A - Async rules run later and reduce transaction response time. [Application User Interface]
5. B - Script Includes promote reusable server-side logic. [Application Automation]
6. D - Dictionary entries define field metadata and platform behavior. [Designing and Creating an Application]
7. B - ServiceNow source control integration manages scoped application files and versions. [Managing Applications]
8. A - onChange is designed for field-change behavior on forms. [Application User Interface]
9. D - UI Policies provide declarative form behavior. [Application User Interface]
10. A - A Reference field stores a link to a record on another table. [Designing and Creating an Application]
11. A - Choice fields standardize allowed values and improve reporting. [Designing and Creating an Application]
12. B - GlideAjax provides controlled asynchronous client-to-server calls. [Application User Interface]
13. B - Application properties centralize configuration outside code. [Application Automation]
14. B - Modules are navigation entries within an application menu. [Designing and Creating an Application]
15. A - Table extension supports reuse of fields and behavior through inheritance. [Designing and Creating an Application]
16. C - ServiceNow applications are strongest for structured, repeatable workflows that benefit from platform services. [Designing and
Creating an Application]
17. A - Import sets provide a staging area for external data. [Working with External Data]
