19. A - Debug Security Rules shows ACL evaluation details. [Security and Restricting Access]
20. A - A clear branching strategy helps control parallel development. [Managing Applications]
21. C - Before rules efficiently modify the record being saved. [Application User Interface]
22. C - Module roles control navigation, while ACLs must still protect the data. [Security and Restricting Access]
23. A - Correct field types improve validation, querying, and user experience. [Designing and Creating an Application]
24. D - ACLs enforce server-side access to data and operations. [Security and Restricting Access]
25. A - Robust integrations evaluate status codes and error responses. [Working with External Data]
26. C - Cross-scope privileges control access between scoped applications. [Security and Restricting Access]
27. B - Conflict resolution protects the intended application state. [Managing Applications]
28. C - gs.hasRole() is a server-side role check, though ACL roles should be used directly when possible. [Security and Restricting
Access]
29. D - Business Rules run server-side around record operations. [Application User Interface]
30. A - Focused commits improve traceability and review. [Managing Applications]
31. A - Coalesce fields determine whether a transform updates an existing record or inserts a new one. [Working with External Data]
32. D - Inbound email processing can create or update application records. [Application Automation]
33. B - After rules are suitable for actions that depend on a completed save. [Application User Interface]
34. D - Application scope isolates and protects application artifacts. [Designing and Creating an Application]
35. D - Scheduled Script Executions run server code on a schedule. [Application Automation]
36. C - Transform scripts support server-side import customization. [Working with External Data]
37. D - Reusable actions and subflows improve consistency and maintenance. [Application Automation]
38. A - Flow Designer provides low-code process automation. [Application Automation]
39. B - A junction table is the normalized design for many-to-many relationships. [Designing and Creating an Application]
40. B - ACL evaluation protects access across interfaces, not just forms. [Security and Restricting Access]
