Practice Test 6
50 questions | Suggested time: 70 minutes | Choose one best answer.
1. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for flow testing?
A. Publish directly to production without a test
B. Judge success only by the flow name
C. Test a flow with representative input, inspect each step, and confirm resulting records
D. Disable error handling during validation
2. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for application scope?
A. Scope changes the instance time zone
B. Use global scope so no protections apply
C. Scope automatically grants every role access
D. Use a scoped application to namespace artifacts and control cross-scope access
3. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for number field?
A. Use a String field and rely on users to type numbers correctly
B. Use a Reference field with no target table
C. Use a Journal field for arithmetic
D. Use an Integer, Decimal, or Currency field when numeric operations and validation are needed
4. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for transform scripts?
A. Use transform scripts for controlled import logic that cannot be handled by direct field maps
B. Disable target validation permanently
C. Put credentials in the source file
D. Use client-only g_form methods during a background transform
5. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for coalesce?
A. Use a journal field as a universal key
B. Mark suitable transform map fields as coalesce to identify matching target records
C. Use coalesce only to change form labels
D. Coalesce every field so no record can transform
6. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for delegated development?
A. Grant admin to every contributor
B. Use delegated development permissions to let approved developers work on an application without full admin
C. Use delegated development to expose all global applications
D. Use module visibility as developer authorization
7. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for module visibility?
A. Use a form section to grant access
B. Rely on module roles as the only protection for table records
C. Assign roles to application menus or modules to limit navigation visibility
D. Use list sorting to hide unauthorized data
8. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for code review?
A. Skip review for server-side security scripts
B. Use code review to inspect changes for quality, security, scope, and maintainability
C. Approve changes based only on file count
D. Review only labels and ignore logic

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 48
9. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for server script debugging?
A. Use browser CSS to trace Business Rules
B. Disable all ACLs permanently
C. Use Script Debugger, logs, and appropriate test records to inspect server-side behavior
D. Change production data randomly until it works
10. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for record producer?
A. Use it as a database index
B. Use it only to delete tables
C. Use a Record Producer to let users create records through a catalog-style interface
D. Use it to replace all ACLs
11. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for async rule?
A. Use it when the user must see an immediate blocking error
B. Use an async Business Rule for non-immediate server work that should not delay the user transaction
C. Use it to control module visibility
D. Use it to set mandatory fields in the browser
12. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for pull/conflict?
A. Pull remote changes and resolve source control conflicts carefully before continuing
B. Ignore conflicts and force overwrite every time
C. Resolve conflict by disabling the application
D. Use a UI Policy to merge Git branches
13. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for secure server API?
A. Rely only on disabled browser buttons
B. Perform sensitive validation and authorization on the server even when client checks exist
C. Trust hidden client variables for authorization
D. Send privileged decisions entirely to the client
14. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for form layout?
A. Use Form Designer or form configuration to organize fields, sections, and related lists
B. Use a REST Message to add sections
C. Use an import set to reorder a form
D. Modify the database schema by dragging browser pixels
15. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for dictionary attributes?
A. Put all field behavior in a module title
B. Use only browser CSS to define the data type
C. Configure field behavior through the dictionary entry and appropriate attributes
D. Edit the database directly outside ServiceNow
16. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for protection policy?
A. Use application artifact protection policies appropriately when distributing scoped applications
B. Use them to replace user ACLs
C. Use them to set list pagination
D. Use them to encrypt all network traffic

