17. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for REST testing?
A. Test a REST method with safe sample data and inspect status, headers, and response body
B. Ignore authentication errors and retry endlessly
C. Test destructive calls first in production
D. Treat any HTTP response as success
18. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for before rule?
A. Use a display rule to import CSV data
B. Use an after rule when the value must be written without another update
C. Use a before Business Rule to change the current record before it is saved
D. Use an async rule to block the user immediately
19. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for data model normalization?
A. Separate reusable entities into related tables instead of repeating the same attributes
B. Copy the same customer details into every transaction record
C. Create duplicate tables for each user
D. Store all records in one unstructured text field
20. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for admin override?
A. Understand the ACL admin override setting and test behavior intentionally
B. The setting controls only form color
C. Assume admin override can never be changed
D. Use admin override to grant anonymous access
21. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for commit?
A. Use commits to delete audit history
B. Include passwords to simplify deployment
C. Commit coherent application changes with a meaningful message
D. Commit random partial changes with no context
22. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for recursion avoidance?
A. Use repeated updates to guarantee correctness
B. Disable all Business Rules globally
C. Convert every rule into a client script
D. Avoid unnecessary current.update() calls inside Business Rules on the same record
23. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for schema map?
A. Use Schema Map to visualize table relationships and extensions
B. Use it to encrypt attachments
C. Use it to execute production scripts
D. Use it to impersonate users
24. In a scoped ServiceNow application, which approach is MOST appropriate for Script Include?
A. Put reusable server-side functions in a Script Include
B. Use a module as a function library
C. Duplicate the same function in every Business Rule
D. Store executable code in a choice label

