Practice Test 6 - Answer Key
1. C - Controlled flow tests reveal input, action, and permission problems. [Application Automation]
2. D - Application scope isolates and protects application artifacts. [Designing and Creating an Application]
3. D - Numeric field types support proper sorting, validation, and calculation. [Designing and Creating an Application]
4. A - Transform scripts support server-side import customization. [Working with External Data]
5. B - Coalesce fields determine whether a transform updates an existing record or inserts a new one. [Working with External Data]
6. B - Delegated development provides controlled development access. [Managing Applications]
7. C - Module roles control navigation, while ACLs must still protect the data. [Security and Restricting Access]
8. B - Code review reduces defects and security issues before promotion. [Managing Applications]
9. C - ServiceNow provides server-side debugging and logging tools for controlled troubleshooting. [Application User Interface]
10. C - Record Producers provide a simplified request interface that creates records. [Application User Interface]
11. B - Async rules run later and reduce transaction response time. [Application User Interface]
12. A - Conflict resolution protects the intended application state. [Managing Applications]
13. B - Client controls improve UX but do not replace server-side security. [Security and Restricting Access]
14. A - Form configuration tools control the record form layout. [Application User Interface]
15. C - Dictionary entries define field metadata and platform behavior. [Designing and Creating an Application]
16. A - Protection policies help protect application intellectual property and artifacts. [Security and Restricting Access]
17. A - Integration testing should verify HTTP status and response content. [Working with External Data]
18. C - Before rules efficiently modify the record being saved. [Application User Interface]
19. A - A normalized model reduces duplication and improves consistency. [Designing and Creating an Application]
20. A - The admin override option affects whether admin users automatically pass that ACL. [Security and Restricting Access]
21. C - Focused commits improve traceability and review. [Managing Applications]
22. D - Updating the same record from its Business Rule can cause recursion or extra processing. [Application Automation]
23. A - Schema Map helps developers inspect a data model visually. [Designing and Creating an Application]
24. A - Script Includes promote reusable server-side logic. [Application Automation]
25. B - Data-driven recipient configuration is safer and easier to maintain. [Application Automation]
26. B - A meaningful display value makes referenced records understandable. [Designing and Creating an Application]
27. D - Choice fields standardize allowed values and improve reporting. [Designing and Creating an Application]
28. C - Display rules can prepare server data before a form is shown. [Application User Interface]
29. D - GlideAjax provides controlled asynchronous client-to-server calls. [Application User Interface]
30. C - Modules are navigation entries within an application menu. [Designing and Creating an Application]
31. C - Least privilege reduces unnecessary access and risk. [Security and Restricting Access]
32. A - REST Messages organize outbound REST integration configuration. [Working with External Data]
33. C - Client-callable Script Includes should expose only validated, necessary data. [Application Automation]
34. B - Correct field types improve validation, querying, and user experience. [Designing and Creating an Application]
35. B - After rules are suitable for actions that depend on a completed save. [Application User Interface]
36. B - Application Access settings define permitted operations from other scopes. [Security and Restricting Access]
37. A - Field ACLs enforce server-side field access. [Security and Restricting Access]
38. A - A clear branching strategy helps control parallel development. [Managing Applications]
39. B - Auto-numbering provides consistent human-readable identifiers. [Designing and Creating an Application]
40. A - Scheduled Script Executions run server code on a schedule. [Application Automation]
41. A - Business Rules run server-side around record operations. [Application User Interface]
42. A - Execution details show inputs, steps, and errors for troubleshooting. [Application Automation]

Unofficial ServiceNow CAD mock exam - original practice questionsPage 55
43. A - Cross-scope privileges control access between scoped applications. [Security and Restricting Access]
44. C - Browser and platform diagnostics help identify client-side script issues. [Application User Interface]
45. A - Transform Maps control source-to-target field mapping. [Working with External Data]
46. D - Understanding execution timing prevents loops and inconsistent outcomes. [Application Automation]
47. D - Record-aware ACL logic can enforce owner-based access. [Security and Restricting Access]
48. D - Inbound email processing can create or update application records. [Application Automation]
49. B - ACL scripts support contextual server-side authorization. [Security and Restricting Access]
50. D - Event-driven notifications separate business logic from communication. [Application Automation]

